**IaC Snippet for Emergency Cross-Account Trust Role:**

```hcl
resource "aws_iam_role" "emergency_sap_role" {
  name = "SAP-Emergency-Response-Role"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow",
      Principal = {
        AWS = "arn:aws:iam::PROD-ACCOUNT:root"
      },
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole",
      Condition = {
        Bool = { "aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent" = "true" }
      }
    }]
  })
}

resource "aws_vpc_endpoint_service" "sap_privatelink" {
  acceptance_required = true
  network_load_balancer_arns = [aws_lb.sap_nlb.arn]
  allowed_principals = [aws_iam_role.emergency_sap_role.arn]
}
```

**Critical Success Factors:**
- All actions must be logged to CloudTrail with immutable audit trails
- Emergency role assumptions require separate out-of-band approval for production access
- JIT elevation tokens must have strict TTLs (typically 1-4 hours) with automatic expiration
- Key rotation must maintain backward compatibility during transition periods?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses fundamental observability for SAP HANA on AWS, translating SAP metrics into CloudWatch and triggering actionable alerts.

## Key Concepts
- CloudWatch agent for EC2
- CloudWatch dashboards and alarms
- SNS-based alerting
- Minimal IaC (CDK/CFN)

## Code Example
```javascript
// AWS CDK snippet: creates an SNS topic and a CloudWatch alarm for EC2 CPU
const topic = new sns.Topic(this, 'SAPCpuAlarmTopic');
const alarm = new cloudwatch.Alarm(this, 'SAPCpuAlarm', {
  metric: new cloudwatch.Metric({
    namespace: 'AWS/EC2',
    metricName: 'CPUUtilization',
    dimensions: { InstanceId: 'i-0123456789abcdef0' },
  }),
  threshold: 85,
  evaluationPeriods: 1,
  datapointsToAlarm: 1,
  statistic: 'Average',
  treatMissingData: cloudwatch.TreatMissingData.NOT_SET,
});
alarm.addAlarmAction(new actions.SnsAction(topic));
```

